--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,23 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## Features
+
+### JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to inside a JSON document.
+The empty pointer `""` refers to the whole document; any other pointer is a sequence of `/`-prefixed
+reference tokens, with `~1` standing for `/` and `~0` for `~` inside a token.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const document = { orders: [{ "item/id": "A-1" }] };
+resolvePointer(document, "/orders/0/item~1id"); // "A-1"
+```
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not valid RFC 6901 syntax, or when it does not resolve: a
+missing member, an array index out of range (`-` is never a valid index here), or a step into a
+scalar. Only an object's own members are resolved, so inherited names such as `constructor` throw.
+Resolution is a read-only lookup, so the document is never modified.
